summary:
  The relayed-Ogg reader knows TITLE= and title= and no other spelling.

history:
  Vorbis comment field names are case-insensitive. The reader tried TITLE=
  first and title= only when there was none, so an older block in capitals
  outvoted a newer one in lower case (the new artist under the old song), and
  Title= was not found at all. Measured 2026-11-10 against the real helper.

target:
  package/contents/ui/reader.py

find:
      low = blob.lower()

replace:
      low = blob.replace(b"TITLE=", b"title=").replace(b"ARTIST=", b"artist=")

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_reader_oggbuf.py::test_a_field_name_counts_whatever_its_case.
  Line-neutral.
